## Tab rendering fix - 0.0.3

- User screenshot showed no tab headers in 0.0.2. Reproduced with a regression
  assertion: ManualTabControl.Template was null. Derived Avalonia controls need
  StyleKeyOverride => typeof(TabControl) to reuse the Fluent theme.
- The actual rendered results also exposed null item callbacks during list
  recycling. Both result and activity templates now accept a null item.
- Smoke checks now inspect the rendered visual tree: four visible nonzero-sized
  tab headers before selection, no auto-selected role, and selected workspace
  content present. Earlier model-only assertions missed this rendering defect.
- Version metadata and Inno setup advanced to 0.0.3 for the corrected installer.

## Tabs and guided configuration implemented — 2026-09-19

- Current version 0.0.2, aligned .NET metadata, manifest and Inno installer.
- Four explicit workspaces: DTX Core, Workstation, Client, PC inspection. Custom
  TabControl disables Avalonia's automatic first-tab selection. No inferred role.
- NodeWorkspace owns results, filters, activity, report/log paths. MainWindow
  captures the originating workspace for background operations; one global run.
- Real phase progress and stable category/ordinal result IDs replace fake delays.
  Virtualized lists, details, result filters/search, activity diagnostics, clipboard
  and log export. Memory activity capped at 2000; per-run logs remain on disk.
- Cancellation for DNS/TCP and local phase boundaries. Partial node reports keep
  mandatory checklist and unexecuted checks as warnings; PC inventory also reports
  cancellation. Native reads already in progress complete before cancellation.
- ConfigurationWizard has five steps, adapter discovery on demand, editable lists,
  approved identity/DNS/IP/user/path fields, endpoint types, DICOM, manual notes,
  draft network preview and review/explicit save or save-and-run.
- ConfigurationDraft edits a detached JSON tree, preserves unknown properties,
  other roles/common, validates, detects disk conflicts twice, replaces atomically
  and keeps original bytes in a unique backup. Invalid files aren't reset.
- DTX observations use Observed instead of Pass. PC inventory includes local
  adapters/IP/DNS and read errors, without active probes or an inferred Client role.
- HTML reports grouped by category, print styles; PC reports/logs unique per run.
- User guide: docs/desktop-workflow.md. Earlier planning entries below are history.
- Tests cover baseline checks, ownership, tabs/busy/role isolation, wizard navigation,
  unknown-field preservation, conflict/validation safety, backup, partial checklist,
  cancellation, log scope and unique PC output. Windows x64 only.

