### DTX inspection

- New Ispeziona DTX toolbar action requires a manually selected role and observes
  local services/state/PID, candidate processes, owned TCP IPv4/IPv6 listeners and
  connections, local/remote IPs, adapter GUID/IP/DHCP/IPv6 and configured DNS servers.
- Uses read-only GetExtendedTcpTable OWNER_PID_ALL; no shell, port scan or UDP.
  Service PID comes from existing EnumServicesStatusEx. Named/configured candidates
  are distinguished from port-only matches; shared process ownership stays explicit.
- Runs existing mandatory checklist and bounded configured DNS/TCP probes once;
  writes separate Inspection-DTX role/machine/timestamp/id HTML reports.
- Verified native TCP ownership against real loopback listeners for both families,
  ambiguous service ownership, unrelated ports, incomplete reads, report formats
  and UI role/busy guards. Installer version 1.0.5.

### Static IP and disabled IPv6 for every role

- Latest user policy supersedes earlier client exceptions: Core, Workstation and
  Client all require static IPv4 and disabled IPv6 on the selected DTX adapter.
- Removed client DHCP exception and obsolete clientRequiresIpv6Disabled setting.
  Legacy JSON fields cannot disable this mandatory check. No OS/network changes.
- DHCP or observed IPv6 (including link-local) fails. Missing adapter or absence
  of IPv6 addresses without binding evidence remains unverified, not PASS.

