### Mandatory infrastructure checklist and per-node reports

- User supplied mandatory Core/Workstation/Client and inter-node infrastructure
  checklist, now enforced in AGENTS.md, planned checks and result generation even
  with empty config lists. Includes IP, IPv6, hostname baseline, Core/internal DNS,
  VPN/mesh/virtual adapters/hosts, Core service state/application health, workstation
  ACL/operational user and installation admin evidence, client DHCP/IPv6 conditions,
  bidirectional DNS/fallback, traffic/inspection, REST/gRPC/dynamic TCP, conditional
  DICOM 104, AV/EDR inspection and absence of SMB/mapped-drive dependency.
- User explicitly authorized always running DNS/TCP probes with timeout when tests
  are started. This supersedes the previous no-network-during-checks requirement.
  Startup, inference and inventory remain without network probes.
- Per-node `infrastructure` holds adapter GUID, approved hostname, Core name/IPs,
  internal DNS, peers, operational user/directories, services, applicability flags,
  explicit protocol endpoints, timeout/latency thresholds and manual notes.
  Inventory import preserves infrastructure baselines instead of overwriting them.
- DNS uses three system-resolver samples; TCP sends no application payload.
  Default timeout 2000 ms (100..10000), up to 16 peers/16 endpoints and 4 concurrent
  probes. No assumed service ports. Missing configuration stays WARNING.
- Reports explicitly distinguish local observations/probe success from unverified
  application health, remote direction, long-term DNS stability, internal-resolver
  provenance, TLS/DPI, effective operational ACL rights and past install privileges.
  Manual notes never become automatic PASS; applicability flags yield NotApplicable.
- Every test report filename includes node role, machine, UTC timestamp and unique
  ID. HTML/text/JSON summaries mark WARNING-only runs as incomplete.
- Implementation details and limitations: docs/infrastructure-checklist.md.
- Verified: Release solution build with zero warnings/errors; extended regression
  suite (all role checklists, all report formats, baseline preservation, DNS IP
  mismatch, DNS/TCP timeouts with simulated providers, report isolation); real
  local read-only runs for Core/Workstation/Client without configured network targets.
  Windows x64 self-contained publish and Inno compilation succeeded; installer
  updated in installers/WgoDtxNodeCheck-Setup.exe. Real DTX network targets and
  manual/security requirements have not been certified in this environment.

