## Repository

Path:

```text
/Users/yariel/Projects/wgo/wgo-dtx-node-check
```

Project:

```text
WGO DTX Node Check / DtxNodeCheck
```

Primary technology:

- .NET 10
- C#
- Avalonia UI
- Windows-first node checks
- macOS UI/build support for cross-platform testing and packaging

## Original Goal

The user requested a .NET 10 C# console app named `DtxNodeCheck`.

Objective:

- Create a single Windows executable for read-only checks on DTX Studio Clinic
  nodes: Core, Workstation, and Client.
- Use one JSON configuration file with common settings and node-specific
  settings.
- Replace existing PowerShell scripts.

Initial CLI examples requested:

```bash
DtxNodeCheck.exe --config .\dtx-studio-heggendorn.json --node workstation
DtxNodeCheck.exe --config .\dtx-studio-heggendorn.json --node core --report .\DTX-Core-Report.txt
DtxNodeCheck.exe --config .\dtx-studio-heggendorn.json --node client --report .\DTX-Client-Report.json --format json
```

Core constraints:

- Read-only by default.
- Do not modify network, DNS, firewall, services, registry, hosts file, or system
  configuration.
- Do not run PowerShell or shell commands from the app.
- Do not send data over the network.
- Do not write files except when report/log behavior is explicitly requested.
- If a report directory is created, it must be because report generation was
  requested.
- Must work on Windows.
- If run outside Windows, exit or show a clear error.

